-- Pruning: Argo CD marks four objects in lab-hub-argocd as requiring
-- pruning, and all four are Helm hooks, which it runs as hooks and never
-- prunes: ServiceAccount, Role and RoleBinding argocd-redis-secret-init
-- (pre-install,pre-upgrade) and Job dex-restarter (post-install, there since
-- the bootstrap). Nothing was deleted.

-- Workloads: no pod in cert-manager, metrics-server, traefik,
-- homer-dashboard or argocd, on either cluster, was created after the
-- handover began. Every Deployment is ready.

-- Secrets: a hash of each Secret's data on both clusters, taken before run 2
-- and after run 3's syncs. The 16 Secrets that existed before are unchanged.
-- One is new: cert-manager/letsencrypt-staging on the spoke. Under Git the
-- spoke's cert-manager sync had failed ("failed calling webhook
-- webhook.cert-manager.io ... connection refused"); from ConfigHub it
-- succeeded, so the ClusterIssuer exists and cert-manager made its ACME
-- account key.

-- Confirmed on this run: `cub unit set-target` takes <space>/<target>; a
-- first promote that carries no changes marks the unit and goes on, and
-- publish says the variant is already released; one repo-creds Secret scoped
-- by the URL prefix oci://oci.hub.confighub.com/space/lab- lets Argo CD pull
-- every variant's release.
